{{Term/Store|Perfect Guard|Perfect Guards|Series, BotW, TotK, AoC|plural}} are a recurring ability in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK, AoC}}<ref name="Tutorial">{{Cite|{{Big|Perfect Guard}}<br/>Parry at the right time to knock an enemy back.|Ability Controls|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Perfect Guard}}<br/>Parry at the right time to repel enemy attacks.|Special Controls|TotK}}</ref><ref>{{Cite Web|quote= If you have save data for the Legend of Zelda: Breath of the wild game, you can get the in-game Training Sword bonus item. Equip this weapon and you’ll automatically hold a Pot Lid as a shield. This combo may also trigger the occasional Perfect Guard! |author= Nintendo |published= |retrieved= October 5, 2021 |url= https://www.nintendo.com/games/detail/hyrule-warriors-age-of-calamity-switch/ |title= Hyrule Warriors: Age of Calamity |site= Nintendo |type= }}</ref>

==Overview==
==={{BotW|-}}===
A Perfect Guard can be performed with any [[Shield]] the moment before an [[Enemy]]'s attack lands by pressing the A-button.<ref name="Tutorial"/> Executing a Perfect Guard temporarily stumbles the Enemy, allowing for [[Link]] to quickly counter the attack. It may also disarm the Enemy. It also works on certain projectiles to be deflected right back at them, such as [[Guardian]] laser beams.

==={{TotK|-}}===
{{Stub|TotK}}
Link can Perfect Guard the [[Rock]]s thrown by [[Bokoblin]]s and [[Soldier Construct]]s.

==Other Appearances==
==={{AoC|-}}===
{{Noncanon|Start}}
In {{AoC}}, characters with shields (such as Link and [[Urbosa]]) can perform Perfect Guards in the same manner as in {{BotW}}, albeit with the Y button instead of the A button. Simply using a Perfect Guard will damage [[Enemy|Enemies]] slightly, even if an attack is not parried. Perfect Guarding a large Enemy will slightly damage their [[Weak Point Gauge]], and cause it to appear for a short time, allowing the player to damage it further and attempt to perform a [[Weak Point Smash]].
{{Noncanon|End}}

